{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeDirectedSystem"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_mul_ginvLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_mul_ginvLim","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L258-L261","doc":"`g n * ginv n = 1`, when `q * qi = 1`.  This is `MarkovTrace.mul_ginv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ginvLim_mul_gLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ginvLim_mul_gLim","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L253-L256","doc":"`ginv n * g n = 1`, when `q * qi = 1`.  This is `MarkovTrace.ginv_mul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_far","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L241-L249","doc":"**Far commutation.**  `g m * g k = g k * g m` when `k + 1 < m`, obtained by\nreading both generators at level `m + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_braid","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L226-L239","doc":"**Braid.**  `g (m+1) * g m * g (m+1) = g m * g (m+1) * g m`, obtained by\nreading both generators at level `m + 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L219-L224","doc":"**Quadratic.**  `g n * g n = (q - qi) • g n + (q * qi) • 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ginvLim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ginvLim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L207-L215","doc":"The inverse generator `ginv n` read at any level `j > n` of the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L201-L205","doc":"The generator `g n` read at any level `j > n` of the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ginvLim_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ginvLim_mem","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L198-L199","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim_mem","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L195-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ginvLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ginvLim","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L187-L193","doc":"The inverse generator at step `n`: the image of `σ_n⁻¹ = σ_n - (q - qi)·1`.\n\n`σInv` is *defined* unconditionally; it is a two-sided inverse only when\n`q * qi = 1`, which is the hypothesis `hqi` carried by the two lemmas below —\nnot by this definition.  This is the `MarkovTrace.ginv` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.gLim","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L182-L185","doc":"The generator adjoined at step `n`: the image of `σ_n ∈ Hecke K q qi (n+1)`.\nThis is the `MarkovTrace.g` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.H_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.H_mono","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L168-L172","doc":"The range filtration is increasing.  This is the `MarkovTrace.H_mono` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLim_mem_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLim_mem_H","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L164-L166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.mem_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.mem_H","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L160-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.H","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L152-L158","doc":"The **range filtration** of the colimit: `H n` is the image of level `n`.\n\nThis is the `MarkovTrace.H` field.  It is the image, not an isomorphic copy of\n`Hecke K q qi n` — those coincide exactly when `ofLim n` is injective, which is\nthe open question of bean `qou-ejde` and is not assumed anywhere here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₐ_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₐ_comp","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L146-L150","doc":"The algebra maps into the colimit are compatible with the tower maps: going\nup the tower first and then into the colimit is the same as going straight in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₐ_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₐ_apply","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L143-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₐ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₐ","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L139-L141","doc":"Level `n` of the tower, as a `K`-algebra map into the colimit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.instAlgebraHeckeLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.instAlgebraHeckeLim","kind":"instance","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L129-L137","doc":"The colimit is a `K`-algebra.\n\nBuilt from the **existing** `DirectLimit.instModule`, so `•` on `HeckeLim` is the\ncolimit's own scalar action and no diamond is created.  `RingHom.toAlgebra'`\napplied to `ofLim 0 ∘ algebraMap` would also typecheck and is deliberately not\nused: it would introduce a second, propositionally-but-not-definitionally equal\n`SMul K (HeckeLim K q qi)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.mul_smul_comm'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.mul_smul_comm'","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L111-L127","doc":"Scalars pull out of the colimit's multiplication on the right. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.smul_mul_assoc'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.smul_mul_assoc'","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L93-L109","doc":"Scalars pull out of the colimit's multiplication on the left. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₗ_eq_ofLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₗ_eq_ofLim","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The ring map and the linear map into the colimit are the *same* function.\nBoth are `x ↦ ⟦⟨n, x⟩⟧`; this is what lets the algebra axioms below be checked\nby transporting the corresponding identity one level down the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₗ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLimₗ","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L83-L85","doc":"Level `n` of the tower, as a `K`-linear map into the colimit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.ofLim","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L79-L81","doc":"Level `n` of the tower, as a ring map into the colimit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.HeckeLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.HeckeLim","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The colimit of the Iwahori–Hecke tower `Hecke K q qi 0 → Hecke K q qi 1 → ⋯`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.heckeF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimit.heckeF","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimit.lean#L71-L73","doc":"The transition family of the Hecke tower, packaged for `DirectLimit`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}